#######################################################################################################################
# comment this out as an additional safeguard in order to reveal potential time zone related bugs using faked time zone.
# e.g. without it, developer in US can't discover the problem during regular working hour when the UTC date is still the 
#  same as the local date dispite the mismatch; but such flaky tests might start failing if run in other time frame.
# #######################################################################################################################
# TZ=GMT-1  # useful to reveal bug when production uses local while test uses UTC.
# TZ=GMT+23 # useful to reveal bug when production uses UTC while test uses local. (Note: this is in POSIX format, so it actually means 23 hours ahead of GMT instead of behind)
